# TestJavaToCSharpFernflowerFacts: fernflower printed as C# with the modification analysis's and the NullabilityPass's
# facts (NULL_MARKED, since 2026-10-12 KOTLIN), judged by Roslyn (see maddi-run-openjdk's JavaToCSharpRatchet). Lower
# is better for printerCrashes, syntaxErrors, unmappedJdkUses and nullableWarnings, higher for syntaxCleanFiles and
# compilingFiles; `types` must not move. Write a better value here in the commit that earns it.
#
# 2026-10-11, first record, with maddi 50ecbe6a0 (read-only parameters where every caller's argument converts):
# 98 read-only collection parameters (81 IReadOnlyList) and nullable declarations as T?, with the same 182 compiling
# files and the same 38 errors as maddi's fernflower.ratchet without the analysis.
#
# 2026-10-11, C#'s nullable reference types enabled (CSharpFacts.STORED_NULL_MARKED; maddi: csharp-check -nullable,
# locals as T?, no ? on simple enums and structs): 2029 nullable warnings, 1150 of them CS8602 (a dereference of a
# possibly null value), 261 CS8604, 212 CS8625 (null into a non-null array element or field), 119 CS8603. Still 182
# files compile; ClasspathScanner, which did not, has 8 more errors (? on its unmapped JDK types).
#
# 2026-10-12, `!` at a dereference of a value that may be null (maddi CSharpNullability: call results, fields,
# parameters and locals, unless the use-site facts know them non-null; asserted locals' initializers), with the pass
# under Policy.KOTLIN (call results make variables nullable, locals asserted at their declaration): CS8602 1150 -> 13,
# 2029 -> 875 nullable warnings. Still 182 files compile.
#
# 2026-10-12, `!` at an argument that may be null for a parameter that is not nullable, a collection's element or key
# always (maddi CSharpNullability.intoParameter): CS8604 254 -> 15, CS8625 212 -> 187, 875 -> 518 nullable warnings.
#
# 2026-10-12, the declarations' verdicts from the pass's report (the pass does not store them itself: write() is the
# caller's), `!` at returns, array element writes and non-null field assignments, (T?) casts of values that may be
# null: CS8603 116 -> 10, CS8625 187 -> 3, 518 -> 128 nullable warnings.
#
# 2026-10-12, `!` on the operand of an unboxing cast that may be null (maddi 4c6cc3551): CS8629 49 -> 2, CS8605
# 13 -> 0, 128 -> 68 nullable warnings. Still 182 files compile.
#
# 2026-10-12, no ? on unmapped library types (maddi 369d81117): ClasspathScanner's 8 extra errors gone, 38 errors as
# maddi's fernflower.ratchet; T? for nullable type-parameter parameters: 68 -> 62 nullable warnings.
#
# 2026-10-12, nullable library results (object.ToString(), node[k], reflection), ? on class type parameters, (T?) null,
# = null! where C# cannot see the assignment (maddi 3a4a1daf9): 62 -> 42 nullable warnings, CS8602 15 -> 12, CS8604 7 ->
# 5, CS8603 10 -> 1, CS8618 5 -> 0, 2 new CS8766 (E? on an interface's type parameter, E in its implementation).
#
# 2026-10-12, the merged nullability work (maddi-mod c74b6641/6472d988, maddi 7dbf49efe), not the printer: 42 -> 43
# nullable warnings, a CS8601 in VarProcessor where a map value's ! went away; maddi 3855fc420, before the printer's
# next commits, already has it.
#
# 2026-10-13, maddi c2be5f33e: a type parameter that is, or is passed as, a dictionary's key is where K : notnull
# (CS8714): 43 -> 38 nullable warnings.
#
# 2026-10-13, maddi ce6ecea39: notnull dictionary keys through wildcards (CS8714 5 -> 0), measured together with
# the JDK nullability hints from JSpecify's annotated JDK (fd3f8419c, merged in the meantime), which move the
# printer's ! assertions throughout: 38 -> 39 nullable warnings.
#
# 2026-10-14, the parameter preconditions (CodeLaser/maddi#125, maddi-mod#41): non-nullable where the method,
# with its whole override family, needs the value, ! at a caller that may pass null, not where the method's answer
# to null is an IllegalArgumentException (also through a helper or a constructor); and maddi f779bcd8b: ! on a
# call to a method declared T? where the pass proves that call non-null, which C# cannot see: 39 -> 38
# nullable warnings; compiling files unchanged.
#
# 2026-10-14, the compatibility library under #nullable enable (maddi 5a6347e13, CodeLaser/maddi#131), and the printer
# asserting what C# then declares nullable (maddi aad8cd424, cce1665b1: a mapping file's ->?, locals the analysis
# finds not null after containsKey, casts to a method's type parameter): 40 -> 32 nullable warnings (devel had 40
# against this file's 39), CS8602 11 -> 7, CS8601 5 -> 3, CS8604 7 -> 5. Still 182 files compile, 36 errors.
#
# Merged on 2026-10-14: the two changes above were each measured alone, from the same base; together not yet.
# The ceiling is ws/maddi-csharp's, the lower one, so a first run of both says whether they add up.
types	199
